# Pinned aggregate sha256 of the ZisK 1.2.0-alpha proving keys that Rome's proofs were made with: provingKey (about 53.7 GB)
# and provingKeySnark (about 27.0 GB). check-keys.sh checks them against this file before every prover start; see its
# header for the format and the hash recipe. File names are sorted bytewise (LC_ALL=C), so a pin does not depend on the
# locale of the host that checks it.
#
# The *.consttree files under provingKey are not hashed. ziskup generates them on the host when it installs the key (a
# GPU install writes them its own way), so they are left out of the hash; each proof's local verify still uses them.
#
# These are the keys that `ziskup -v 1.2.0-alpha --provingkey` and `ziskup setup_snark` install (see docs/PROVER-HOST.md).
# A different ZisK release has different keys: do not re-pin to make a mismatch go away, install the release this file was
# made for. Pin a key set of your own, on purpose, with:
#   ZISK_HOME=<where the keys are> MANIFEST=./prover/keys.sha256 bash ./prover/check-keys.sh --write
7200c160f249ce49ab16ec00fa566210b6ec24ecc407ed402e4241e739c113b4  provingKey
71056920ca412beed123096ebfcd764159534cf8f182b5832ec0f563fb56e912  provingKeySnark
